<BaseLayout title="About | Canada2080" description="About the Canada2080 initiative, its provenance, and its publication standards.">
  <section class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">Initiative record / 04</p><h1>About Canada2080</h1><p>A public national initiative helping investors, institutions, and policy leaders build Canadian-controlled capability for a changing planet.</p></section>
  <section class="section shell split-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">What we do</p><h2>Connect evidence to accountable coalition-building.</h2></div><div class="reading-column"><p>Canada2080 combines evidence, historical learning, scenario work, public narrative, regional missions, and accountable coalition-building. The 2080 horizon is an ambition and a scenario boundary used to guide present decisions.</p><p>Waterloo is one field case within a wider national record. It does not stand as a national template.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section shell split-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Provenance</p><h2>The Five Gaps originate with Francis Wang.</h2></div><div class="reading-column"><EvidenceLabel label="Verified fact" /><p>Canada2080 attributes the Five Canadian Systemic Gaps to Francis Wang's 2025 DDes research proposal, <em>Foresight-Driven Innovation</em>. Later Canada2080 research may update and sharpen the formulation while preserving this provenance.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section shell split-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Publication standard</p><h2>Evidence, consent, and public consequence.</h2></div><div class="reading-column"><p>Before publication, Canada2080 checks source, wording, evidence class, provenance, consent, attribution, privacy, Indigenous and cultural sensitivity, conflicts of interest, image rights, and whether an artifact could be read as an offer, promise, endorsement, or forecast.</p>        <a class="text-link" href="/research">Read the research programme <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
